{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>ואני נסכתי</b> — I have enthroned. The meaning is that he is a נסיך, like \"the five kings of Midian who were princes of Sihon.\" Know that סמיכה sometimes is from the honored to the lowly, and the opposite, like \"You are the king of Elohim.\"" "<b>ואני נסכתי מלכי</b> — YHWH is his portion, and they are Your people and Your portion, and similarly להשתחות למלך ה' צבאות — that he is the anointed one, in the manner of \"and all kings shall bow to him,\" for if it had been on the Name [HaShem], the lamed would have a kamatz gadol."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:01.017203093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}